{"id":"5a5b99309397a57a","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence.md","title":"epsilon nfa language equivalence","display":"thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence — epsilon nfa language equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence","display":"thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence — epsilon nfa language equivalence","depends_on":["[[73-df-nfa-notation]]","[[73-df-nfa-acceptance-notation]]","[[73-df-epsilon-nfa-notation]]","[[73-df-epsilon-nfa-acceptance-notation]]","[[73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination]]","[[73-df-finite-words-and-languages]]"],"aliases":["73-thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence","73-theorem-1.2"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§2.5, print pp. 68–78; PDF pp. 90–100; local typed epsilon label","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_numbering":"local-catalog; not book numbering","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§2.4, Theorem 2.2, pp. 24–28; local epsilon-elimination construction","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":2},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence — epsilon nfa language equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"222bbfa3171233c2\" href=\"?note=222bbfa3171233c2\" title=\"73-df-nfa-notation\">73-df-nfa-notation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"52ddba8829989be5\" href=\"?note=52ddba8829989be5\" title=\"73-df-nfa-acceptance-notation\">73-df-nfa-acceptance-notation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a33552223dc0fdf0\" href=\"?note=a33552223dc0fdf0\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-nfa-notation\">73-df-epsilon-nfa-notation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4ffa4d7b72a6a19e\" href=\"?note=4ffa4d7b72a6a19e\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-nfa-acceptance-notation\">73-df-epsilon-nfa-acceptance-notation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c045448153929107\" href=\"?note=c045448153929107\" title=\"73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination\">73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"0a6da8c909717780\" href=\"?note=0a6da8c909717780\" title=\"73-df-finite-words-and-languages\">73-df-finite-words-and-languages</a></span></div>"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-epsilon-nfa-language-equivalence</span><span>73-theorem-1.2</span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§2.5, print pp. 68–78; PDF pp. 90–100; local typed epsilon label"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_numbering","html":"local-catalog; not book numbering"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§2.4, Theorem 2.2, pp. 24–28; local epsilon-elimination construction"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"2"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>固定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> 满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\\)</span>；有限词、单字符词和拼接见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"0a6da8c909717780\" href=\"?note=0a6da8c909717780\" title=\"73-df-finite-words-and-languages\">73-df-finite-words-and-languages</a>。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>两种机器类和其接受语言使用以下直接依赖中固定的同一字母表实例。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NFA}=\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\mathrm{NFA}=\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varepsilon\\mathrm{}\\mathrm{NFA}=\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\varepsilon\\mathrm{}\\mathrm{NFA}=\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> 分别使用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"222bbfa3171233c2\" href=\"?note=222bbfa3171233c2\" title=\"73-df-nfa-notation\">73-df-nfa-notation</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"a33552223dc0fdf0\" href=\"?note=a33552223dc0fdf0\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-nfa-notation\">73-df-epsilon-nfa-notation</a> 的同一固定字母表实例。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}1.2}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;((\\exists M\\in \\varepsilon\\mathrm{}\\mathrm{NFA}\\;L=L(M))\\leftrightarrow(\\exists M\\in \\mathrm{NFA}\\;L=L(M)))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}1.2}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;((\\exists M\\in \\varepsilon\\mathrm{}\\mathrm{NFA}\\;L=L(M))\\leftrightarrow(\\exists M\\in \\mathrm{NFA}\\;L=L(M)))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>按有限子集状态构造（以及需要时先取空转移闭包）得到保持接受语言的有限自动机；类与语言均在假设所列定义中确定。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"